  "headline_index": null,
  "what_the_study_did": "The study evaluated the cardiotoxic effects of vanoxerine using two different nonclinical new approach methodologies (NAMs): a complex cardiac microphysiological system (MPS) and a human-induced pluripotent stem cell-derived cardiomyocyte (hiPSC-CM) multi-electrode array (MEA) CiPA model.",
  "what_it_found": "Vanoxerine treatment delayed repolarization and induced early afterdepolarization-like events in both NAMs, consistent with a predicted increased risk of torsades de pointes (TdP). The study also quantified significant drug loss of vanoxerine due to binding within the MPS.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "These findings demonstrate cardiac NAMs have the potential to be used for safety and efficacy assessment with the advantage of minimizing the use of animal models.",
      "topic": "NAMs utility"
    },
    {
      "quote": "Our report is the first study that systematically quantifies vanoxerine proarrhythmia (i.e., TdP) potential in multiple cardiac NAMs.",
      "topic": "Novelty of study"
    },
    {
      "quote": "Nonspecific binding resulted in significant drug loss (99%) observed for vanoxerine in the complex cardiac MPS for all concentrations tested ( Table 2 ).",
      "topic": "Drug loss"
    },
    {
      "quote": "Taken together, the current study demonstrates that nonclinical cardiac NAMs can recapitulate clinical outcomes and predict vanoxerine-induced delayed repolarization and TdP risk categorization in vitro.",
      "topic": "NAMs recapitulation"
    },
    {
      "quote": "The hiPSC-CM MEA CiPA model is a validated [ 22 ], high-throughput tool that enables rapid evaluation of drug-induced electrophysiological effects in 2D monolayers.",
      "topic": "MEA model"
    },
    {
      "quote": "The cardiac MPS described here provides the capability to sequentially measure membrane voltage, intracellular calcium, and contractility by offering a comprehensive view of how drugs may disrupt the tightly linked processes involved in EC coupling [ 3 , 5 ], albeit at lower throughput.",
      "topic": "MPS model"
    }
